  "Thank you, your home is lovely.": "content/audio/thank-you-your-home-is-lovely-d8185fe2.m4a",
  "It's a small place.": "content/audio/it-s-a-small-place-2b33fba5.m4a",
  "My sister tells me you found our family's name in an old ledger.": "content/audio/my-sister-tells-me-you-found-our-family--eeea68b3.m4a",
  "Yes, and an old photo too.": "content/audio/yes-and-an-old-photo-too-42a82de7.m4a",
  "No, that's not right.": "content/audio/no-that-s-not-right-2e365e66.m4a",
  "I remember that house. Let me tell you about it.": "content/audio/i-remember-that-house-let-me-tell-you-ab-2e4f714c.m4a",
  "Please, I'd love to hear it.": "content/audio/please-i-d-love-to-hear-it-bf48b497.m4a",
  "Only if it's short.": "content/audio/only-if-it-s-short-64a5436f.m4a",
  "We arrived here with very little money. Our parents worked two jobs each. It wasn't easy, but that little house became our whole world.": "content/audio/we-arrived-here-with-very-little-money-o-f21a24a8.m4a",
  "That sounds like a hard beginning.": "content/audio/that-sounds-like-a-hard-beginning-f125dc6a.m4a",
  "That must have taken real strength.": "content/audio/that-must-have-taken-real-strength-ebb34426.m4a",
  "It was hard, yes. But we weren't alone. Neighbors shared food with us. Someone taught our mother English on weekends.": "content/audio/it-was-hard-yes-but-we-weren-t-alone-nei-a9eee789.m4a",
  "People really took care of each other.": "content/audio/people-really-took-care-of-each-other-ac125433.m4a",
  "That happens everywhere.": "content/audio/that-happens-everywhere-c57adf0c.m4a",
  "Exactly. And that's why we always write letters — to remember who helped us.": "content/audio/exactly-and-that-s-why-we-always-write-l-3c249c28.m4a",
  "Is that why letters matter so much to you?": "content/audio/is-that-why-letters-matter-so-much-to-yo-21224e01.m4a",
  "I never write letters, sorry.": "content/audio/i-never-write-letters-sorry-3ebb5178.m4a",
  "Yes. Some of those old letters are still in that house, I think.": "content/audio/yes-some-of-those-old-letters-are-still--f5a74906.m4a",
  "Can we go check the house sometime?": "content/audio/can-we-go-check-the-house-sometime-4d0a01b8.m4a",
  "That house is probably gone.": "content/audio/that-house-is-probably-gone-92b2c96e.m4a",
  "We can. But first, let me finish. We didn't want to leave that house. We had to — the rent became too high for us.": "content/audio/we-can-but-first-let-me-finish-we-didn-t-f8a5ec91.m4a",
  "That's such a hard choice to make.": "content/audio/that-s-such-a-hard-choice-to-make-1a024767.m4a",
  "That's not fair at all.": "content/audio/that-s-not-fair-at-all-2ca2e0a8.m4a",
  "It was. But we promised each other something before we left.": "content/audio/it-was-but-we-promised-each-other-someth-0cdd774f.m4a",
  "What did you promise?": "content/audio/what-did-you-promise-2a3c0041.m4a",
  "I don't need details.": "content/audio/i-don-t-need-details-5d0925ee.m4a",
  "We promised to come back one day, together, as a family.": "content/audio/we-promised-to-come-back-one-day-togethe-b4646313.m4a",
  "That's a promise worth keeping.": "content/audio/that-s-a-promise-worth-keeping-8dbd5a42.m4a",
  "Promises don't always work out.": "content/audio/promises-don-t-always-work-out-57d1f5a6.m4a",
  "One neighbor helped us more than anyone. A young woman who ran a small shop nearby.": "content/audio/one-neighbor-helped-us-more-than-anyone--1b1e3385.m4a",
  "Do you remember her name?": "content/audio/do-you-remember-her-name-a7d5e19c.m4a",
  "That's not important now.": "content/audio/that-s-not-important-now-1581ff00.m4a",
  "It's been so long... but I think her shop sold books.": "content/audio/it-s-been-so-long-but-i-think-her-shop-s-d4c31445.m4a",
  "Emma's shop sells books too.": "content/audio/emma-s-shop-sells-books-too-2eec80ab.m4a",
  "That's probably not related.": "content/audio/that-s-probably-not-related-5bf47b18.m4a",
  "Wait — could it be the same shop? Ten Letters?": "content/audio/wait-could-it-be-the-same-shop-ten-lette-e64f36db.m4a",
  "I'll ask Emma about it tomorrow.": "content/audio/i-ll-ask-emma-about-it-tomorrow-95ce8689.m4a",
  "It's probably just a coincidence.": "content/audio/it-s-probably-just-a-coincidence-4a7ba60f.m4a",
  "This all matters because my sister carried this story alone for years.": "content/audio/this-all-matters-because-my-sister-carri-507b95a3.m4a",
  "She doesn't have to carry it alone anymore.": "content/audio/she-doesn-t-have-to-carry-it-alone-anymo-d9ee30ad.m4a",
  "That sounds dramatic.": "content/audio/that-sounds-dramatic-405fefc3.m4a",
  "Thank you for saying that.": "content/audio/thank-you-for-saying-that-4db2ea2e.m4a",
  "Thank you for trusting me with it.": "content/audio/thank-you-for-trusting-me-with-it-477b42b5.m4a",
  "It's really no problem.": "content/audio/it-s-really-no-problem-7a7e3643.m4a",
  "Let's go visit that house together soon, all three of us.": "content/audio/let-s-go-visit-that-house-together-soon--b86e5c1c.m4a",
  "I'd love that. Let's plan it.": "content/audio/i-d-love-that-let-s-plan-it-a7c71db4.m4a",
  "Maybe some other time.": "content/audio/maybe-some-other-time-ecc99026.m4a",
